  "construction_decisions": [
    "Rebuilt the major cloth shell from a fitted open torso grid and two matched 40-edge armhole boundaries. The existing baseline was already joined; the purpose was better tangents and curvature, not claiming to close an open seam.",
    "Used five cubic sleeve-cap rows and three shoulder/yoke rows, removed the old 42/40 zipper correspondence and concentrated underarm crease. Retained cuff world placement and the lower sleeve construction direction.",
    "Used one connected collar cross-section from standing neck band over the rounded turn to the outward leaf; front endpoints are lowered and moved outward, with actual evaluated-surface clearance.",
    "Built curved lapel facing strips from the fitted front edge, with a 7 mm softened roll, instead of two planar polygons.",
    "Refit existing shoulder tabs and their piping, repositioned the lapel snaps onto their faces, and regenerated tonal seam tubes from projected centerlines.",
    "Changed only Main cloth, Interior lining and Seams thread materials. Original separate Strap, Piping and Hardware materials remain exact."
  ],
  "selection_semantics": "Main body object name retained but its mesh/vertex indices rebuilt. Old Body/Sleeve groups replaced by Body panels | rebuilt fitted shell, L/R Sleeve | rebuilt editable region, L/R Armhole | shared 40-edge seam. Former separate pointed-front collar cloth objects removed; their shape is now part of the stand/turned-leaf object. Cuff and ornament object names/geometry remain usable.",
